(International Student Guide - Example University of Applied Sciences \(fictional sample) '
(document\)) '
() '
(Before you arrive) '
() '
(Non-EU/EEA students need a residence permit for studies if they stay longer than 90 days.) '
(Apply online as soon as you receive your admission letter and pay the application fee.) '
(Processing normally takes one to three months, so apply early. You must visit a service) '
(point to prove your identity and give your fingerprints. Bring your passport, the) '
(admission letter and proof of funding.) '
() '
(Proof of funding: Students must show that they have at least 800 euros per month for) '
(living costs, for example a bank statement covering the first year.) '
() '
(Tuition fees) '
() '
(Students from outside the EU/EEA pay a tuition fee of 10,000 euros per academic year for) '
(English-taught bachelor's programmes. EU/EEA students do not pay tuition fees.) '
(Scholarships that cover 50 percent or 100 percent of the fee are available based on) '
(admission results. Apply for the scholarship in the same application form as your study) '
(place.) '
() '
ET
