(Housing) '
() '
(The student housing foundation offers furnished rooms and shared apartments close to) '
(campus. Rents range from 380 to 620 euros per month. Apply for housing as soon as you have) '
(accepted your study place, since popular apartments fill up quickly. A deposit equal to) '
(one month's rent is required. The private rental market is more expensive and often) '
(requires a security deposit of up to two months' rent.) '
() '
(Arrival and orientation) '
() '
(Orientation week takes place one week before the autumn semester begins. Attendance is) '
(strongly recommended. During the week you will receive your student card, activate your) '
(user account, meet your tutor and learn about the campus. A free airport pick-up service) '
(is available on the two Saturdays before orientation if you register at least two weeks in) '
(advance.) '
() '
(Registering your stay: If you are staying longer than three months, you must register your) '
(address with the local register office. Registration gives you a personal identity code,) '
(which you need to open a bank account.) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
