(Working during your studies) '
() '
(Students with a residence permit for studies may work up to 30 hours per week during the) '
(semester. There is no weekly limit during holidays. Practical training and thesis work) '
(arranged as part of your degree do not count towards the limit. Working more than the) '
(permitted hours can affect your permit renewal.) '
() '
(After graduation) '
() '
(If you wish to stay in the country after graduating, you can apply for an extended permit) '
(to look for work or start a business. The permit is valid for up to two years. Apply) '
(before your current permit expires. The career services team runs CV clinics, interview) '
(training and employer events every term.) '
() '
(Finnish language courses) '
() '
(Free beginner Finnish courses are offered for international students each semester.) '
(Courses are worth 3 ECTS credits and can be included in your free-choice studies. Enrol) '
(through the course enrolment system at the same time as other courses.) '
() '
ET
endstream
